{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120424","id":3895412547,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7oL0dD","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120424","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120424.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120424.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120424","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120424/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120424/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120424/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2d9e3cc8608d42465074447f9701b73224f99c80","number":120424,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add angular lock (rigid weld / fixed joint) option to PinJoint2D","user":{"login":"Marenz","id":424752,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNDc1Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/424752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz","html_url":"https://github.com/Marenz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Addresses godotengine/godot-proposals#86\n\nAdds an optional rigid angular lock to `PinJoint2D`, turning the pin from a free hinge into a rigid weld: the two pinned bodies keep their own collision shapes but a fixed relative orientation, so they move and topple as one rigid unit. This is the 2D \"Glue Joint\" / \"Fixed Joint\" requested in proposal #86 — a `PinJoint2D` already locks relative *position*; this adds the relative *rotation* lock, completing a fixed joint for 2D.\n\nNew API on `PinJoint2D`:\n\n- `angular_lock_enabled: bool` (default `false`) — enable the rigid weld.\n- `angular_lock_softness: float` (default `0.0`) — how quickly the weld restores its locked orientation; `0` snaps back in one step, higher springs back more softly (same sense as `softness`).\n- `angular_lock_play: float` (default `0.0`) — angular deadzone (radians); the weld heals back toward alignment but stops this much short, leaving a tunable permanent free play.\n\nPlumbed through `PhysicsServer2D` as a new `PinJointFlag` (`PIN_JOINT_FLAG_ANGULAR_LOCK_ENABLED`, appended = value 2) and two `PinJointParam`s (`PIN_JOINT_ANGULAR_LOCK_SOFTNESS`, `_PLAY`).\n\nImplementation:\n\nThe 2D pin solver is single-phase (velocity only). A restoring term on the real velocity channel is unstable: there is nowhere to bleed the injected correction energy, so under sustained load the relative angle walks past ±π and settles flipped 180°. So this uses a Box2D-style split impulse:\n\n1. The real velocity channel drives the relative angular velocity → 0 (kills spin, injects no energy, never flips).\n2. The biased (pseudo-velocity) channel — the same split-impulse channel the contact solver uses for penetration recovery, reset every step in `integrate_forces`, integrated into orientation in `integrate_velocities` — carries the restoring term, healing the residual angle geometrically without it becoming real spin.\n\nNew helper `GodotBody2D::apply_bias_torque_impulse()`. Heal fraction per step is `1/(1+softness)` (≤1, so no overshoot); `play` is subtracted from the error magnitude before healing.\n\nHow tested:\n\nTested extensively in 2D scenes with real falling/colliding `RigidBody2D` bodies. With two boxes welded:\n\n- Rigid (`softness=0`): after an external knock rotates one body ~86° out of alignment, the relative angle recovers to <1° within ~2 physics frames and the bodies thereafter move as one unit.\n- Softness sweep: recovery time increases monotonically with `softness` (snap-back at `0`, progressively softer spring-back for higher values), always settling back to the locked orientation.\n- Play: with `angular_lock_play` set, the weld settles at exactly that residual angle instead of fully realigning.\n- No flip: the relative angle never runs away to ±180°, including under sustained gravity load on a cantilevered (overhanging) welded pair and under repeated hard knocks.\n- Chains of welded bodies remain stable at arbitrary length.\n\nThis PR was developed with AI assistance and tested extensively by me; all code was reviewed by me and no copyrighted/copied code was introduced.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,